# Every script here runs on the Linux host, never on whatever machine edited
# it. A CRLF shebang line is a silent "bad interpreter" failure at exec time,
# not a diff-noise annoyance -- force LF regardless of any given clone's own
# core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf

# Vendored, unedited-by-us third-party assets -- byte-exact fidelity matters
# (xterm.js is a single ~488KB minified line; CRLF conversion on core.
# autocrlf=true would silently corrupt it rather than error loudly).
# Explicit -text, not relying on git's own binary-detection heuristic.
orchestrator/internal/dashboard/static/vendor/* -text
